### Full M2 pairing dance (run against https://somatriq.mokka-dev.de)

### 0. First-run check — which wizard branch?
GET /api/v1/auth/status
# → { "has_account": false }

### 1. Claim the local account (only while zero accounts exist)
POST /api/v1/auth/register
{
  "username": "owner",
  "password": "a-long-personal-passphrase"
}
# → { "access_token": "…", "token_type": "bearer", "expires_at": "…" }

### 2. Login (subsequent runs)
POST /api/v1/auth/login
{ "username": "owner", "password": "…" }
# → TokenResponse

### 3. Web creates a pairing session (account JWT)
POST /api/v1/pairing/sessions
Authorization: Bearer <account JWT>
# → { "session_id": "…", "pairing_code": "7KQ2M9XW", "expires_at": "…" }

### 4. Wizard polls status
GET /api/v1/pairing/sessions/{session_id}
Authorization: Bearer <account JWT>
# → { "status": "pending" | "consumed", "device": {…} }

### 5. Collector exchanges the code (no auth — code possession is the proof)
POST /api/v1/pairing/confirm
{
  "pairing_code": "7KQ2M9XW",
  "device_name": "pixel-8-owner"
}
# → { "device_id": "…", "token": "sqt_dev_…", "token_type": "device",
#     "scopes": ["ingest.write","device.read","sync.read"], "issued_at": "…" }

### 6. Collector ingests with its device token
POST /api/v1/ingest/batches
Authorization: Bearer sqt_dev_…
{ … ingest-batch-v2.example.json … }
# → ack with "raw_ack": true  ← the ONLY prune authorization

### 7. Web lists devices / revokes a lost phone
GET /api/v1/devices
POST /api/v1/devices/{device_id}/revoke
